[Music]  president fest riots dear annie marie  sipkes  dear rupert wood distinguished guests  thank you very much for inviting me to  speak here at the  ftth conference it's a great pleasure to  welcome you all here in austria  the past two years since the kobit  outbreak  haven't been easy at all  so i'm very glad indeed to meet you here  all in person  and i'm also very happy that even a  delegation from the ukraine is attending  the conference  home schooling  working from home video conferencing  online shopping  e-government streaming films  deco with pandemic  has hugely increased demands on digital  infrastructures  we have seen the importance of digital  infrastructure rise  both  at work  and at home  and we all need the fast and stable  internet connection  and now the time has come to drive  forward the digital decade  which is only possible with a stable  broadband connection as you all know  austria has a very good coverage 91  of all households have at least 30  megabits per second and 50 percent  have already a gigabit connection  as the federal government  we have therefore set ourselves  ambitious goal  providing austria  with nationwide fixed  and mobile gigabit connection by 2030.  for this we have a concrete plan  first  at least 60 percent of austrian  households will be upgraded privately by  companies  the telecommunication act has created  investment friendly conditions here  austria completed the national  implementation of the european  electronic communications code in  october 2021  the relevant law the so-called tkg  includes a large number of provisions  covering all areas of telecommunications  one important part is  the creation of incentives for  investments in high-speed broadband  networks  because the demands on the electronic  communication networks are constantly  growing this has been achieved by  simplifying cooperation and  co-investment agreements and the  sector-specific laws  secondly  frequency allocations of mobile  communication  broad coverage obligations were imposed  on operators for the rapid  monetary  rollout in underserved areas in the  countryside  as a result  of these coverage obligations around  1  700 towns and villages will receive  nationwide high performance mobile  broadband coverage by 2023  this means that by 2030  we will be able to cover 80 percent of  these areas  thirdly  the remaining areas  there are for the remaining areas there  are public subsidies  since 2015  we have invested more than a billion  euros in broadband expansion reaching  1.1 million citizens and supporting a  rollout in nearly  400 towns and villages this has in turn  triggered investments of 2.5 billion  euros  with the new framework of the initiative  broadband austria 2030  a total  of 1.4 billion additional funds will be  available until 2026.  with our second so-called broadband  billion we will take a huge step to  achieve our goal  however  especially in the countryside expansion  is difficult and of course is no  expensive  that is why we are starting the  broadband turbo with the second  broadband billion  we can make even better use for  digitalization through good digital  infrastructure we can create equal  opportunities in the regions  you have to know that around 40 percent  of the austin population live in  non-urban areas  people should be free to choose where  they live  broadband expansion  is also crucial for an attractive  business location  if we want to remain competitive we must  invest in digital infrastructure  make austria even more livable  through digitalization  nevertheless  we all have to act together to reach our  ambitious goal of nationwide fixed and  mobile gigabit connection by 2030.  every euro  we invest in digital infrastructure  is investment in the future  in quality of life  and in competitiveness  i'm very much looking forward to my new  task of leading austria one further step  into the digitalized world thank you  very much  [Applause]  [Music]  you

